The forwarding door requires: "Ze owns only what it marked."
See ai/doors/forwarding.md, "Who depends on it from outside".

The system FIB needs a live IPv4 route identity receipt before reasserting
unchanged forwarding. An ownership decision cannot use a process-local cache.
Linux 7.3 fib_table_insert answers EEXIST for an exact fib_info and route key,
or ENOENT otherwise, when CREATE, REPLACE, EXCL and APPEND are all absent.
IPv6 must be refused before sending: fib6_add_rt2node can insert a route or
update duplicate expiry/MTU even without the creation flags.

The method reuses the upstream route encoder and existing handle. Only ACK is
requested; none of the four mutation flags is present. Invalid route inputs
and IPv6 are refused before constructing a netlink request.

